  "caption": "Nine months after a knee reconstruction, Quinn circled game day on the calendar. Cleared, so ready, right? One wobbly hop test later, Kay pulled out the clipboard.\n\nReturning to sport after an ACL reconstruction should depend on objective readiness, not just the calendar or clearance alone. Re-injury risk tends to be highest in the first year back.\n\nWhat can help: respecting a minimum time frame (often around 9 months, as guided by your team), building quad strength to near 90% of the other side, hop tests close to 90% symmetry, good landing control when tired, and checking you feel mentally ready.\n\nGet it checked if the knee swells after hard sessions or feels like it's giving way.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
